lly pins them or whether they'd route successfully (making their removal from durable state a regression).The research side is internally consistent (pinned set covers the moved rows except `manualStop`/`pivot_confirm_accepted`/`dry_run_halt`, which have no stem anyway — bookkeeping avoids spurious exit-1 halts). For review, let me check what the synthesis closeout emits and confirm no stem-form appends exist in the review YAMLs.Writing iteration 1 artifacts now.Now the canonical iteration state record — timestamp from the clock, then append via the gateway.Iteration 1 complete: config row + iteration row projected. Updating progress and starting iteration 2 — `sk-git` scripts/hooks.Reading the new enforcement machinery — the gate hook and the message contract.The gate hook looks solid. Reading the rest of the contract validator.Contracts look internally consistent. Let me empirically test the `-am` bundling gap in `evaluateCommand`.The README says Pi resolves imports against the symlink path `.pi/extensions/` — so `../../.skilled/...` resolves from repo root. Let me verify the symlink exists.The symlink-layout resolution is correct in production, but the vitest suite imports the real file — let me verify whether the test's dynamic imports resolve or silently fail-open.Pi gate tests pass via the vitest alias — the symlink-layout design is coherent. Let me run the message-contract test suite too.Tests all pass. Let me scan `validate-message.mjs`'s rev-list path and the pre-push hook diff before closing iteration 2.The README describes a new `commit-msg` gate and a pre-push message-contract gate. Let me check the actual hook implementations.The commit-msg hook is carefully fail-soft/fail-closed. Now the pre-push message-contract gate — the rev-list computation is where correctness risk lives.`BARE_IN_SUBCOMMAND` only affects `add -u`/`restore -s` — the bundle gap stands. Last check: leaf-manifest/aliases entries resolve to real files.Manifest/aliases clean — 71/71 res